  "title": "Juana Azurduy",
  "summary": "A woman from Upper Peru (present-day Bolivia), she joined the 1809 Chuquisaca revolution with her husband Padilla, who died in battle in 1816 after she was wounded at La Laguna. She was made lieutenant colonel in 1816 and later promoted to colonel by Simon Bolivar. She died poor in Jujuy in 1862; Argentina promoted her to general in 2009. Her birth year is given as 1780 or 1781.",
